  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "20260909T192849Z",
      "ts": "2026-09-09T19:28:49Z",
      "title": "Carrier 'Forget' only hid locally; shared_carrier_tombstones was dead",
      "lesson": "1.1.46 gave Carrier its own shared_carriers/shared_carrier_tombstones tables (parity with shared_contacts), but _SharedNameDirectory only ever implemented fetchNames()+remember() \u2014 no forget(). The Carrier field's 'Forget this value' button called the generic local-only hideRememberedMemory (SharedPreferences), same as Customer/Location, so a forgotten carrier kept reappearing on other devices/apps and the tombstone table was never written to. Person names already had true cross-device forget via the separate contact_sync.dart path. Fixed: added forget() to _SharedNameDirectory (delete row + upsert tombstone), exposed on SharedCarriersClient/SharedContactsClient, wired CarrierSuggestionField to call it (best-effort) before the local hide so the UI still responds instantly if offline.",
      "do_not_regress": "Any new shared_* directory (values+tombstones pair) must expose and wire a real forget() \u2014 do not ship a tombstones table that nothing ever inserts into. 'Forget this value' must mean the same thing (cross-app, cross-device) for every field that claims a shared directory, not just person names.",
      "case_ids": [
        "carrier_forget_cross_app"
      ],
      "tags": [
        "contacts",
        "carrier",
        "shared-directory"
      ]
    }
  ],
